  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><strong>Aura</strong> faint enchantment; <strong>CL</strong> 5th<br>\n<strong>Slot</strong> none; <strong>Price</strong> 200 gp (Weapon), 100 gp (Armor/Shield); <strong>Weight</strong> -</p>\n<p>This device takes many forms depending on the technology of the setting. But usually a small lightweight device that can be easily attached to any kind of gizmo.</p>\n<p>An enchantment infuser can be enhanced as if it were a single type of masterwork armor, shield, or weapon, chosen at the time of the device's creation.</p>\n<p>As a full-round action, this device can be attached/detached to an appropriate armor, shield, or weapon gizmo (as though attaching a modification gizmo). The attached armor, shield, or weapon gains the enchantment infuser’s magic item properties (enhancement value, special weapon or armor abilities, etc.).</p>\n<p>Equipment cannot gain properties that they could not normally gain using an enchantment infuser, such as impact on a ranged weapon, or brawling on medium or heavy armor. If the gizmo has its own enhancement bonus or has already been enhanced as a suit of armor, shield, or a weapon, the enhancement bonuses and special abilities provided by the enchantment infuser do not stack.</p>\n<p>When a user activates the gizmo, they may choose whether they use the gizmo's enchantment bonus and special abilities, or the bonuses provided by the enchantment infuser.</p>\n<p>If the gizmo the enchantment infuser attached to is destroyed, the infuser may be safely salvaged off the remains no worse for wear (excluding events such as being thrown together into a smelting furnace).<br>\n<strong>Construction Requirements</strong><br>\nSmith Magical Weapons And Armor, Enhancement sphere, Tinker sphere; <strong>Cost</strong> Weapon 100 gp; Armor/Shield 50 gp</p>\n<p><a href=\"http://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/practitioner-magic-items#toc3\">Source: Spheres of Power Wiki</a></p>",
